WEBVTT

00:02.480 --> 00:05.350
<b>Sign Language Guide</b>

00:03.330 --> 00:05.350
"Sign Language Guide"?

00:05.810 --> 00:07.670
What... is this?

00:09.640 --> 00:13.160
Is Itsu-kun trying to pick up 
yet another skill?

00:14.000 --> 00:14.990
But...

00:15.910 --> 00:17.800
Why sign language?

01:55.210 --> 01:59.010
What Kind of Voice?

02:01.930 --> 02:05.980
<i>That was the first time I've ever 
gotten home so close to curfew.</i>

02:07.200 --> 02:09.190
<i>A coin from a faraway land...</i>

02:11.200 --> 02:16.260
<i>I feel like it can take me anywhere 
because Itsuomi-san gave it to me.</i>

02:19.350 --> 02:21.020
<i>Oh, Rin-chan!</i>

02:20.990 --> 02:23.330
<b>Rin-chan</b>

02:20.990 --> 02:23.330
I haven't seen Itsuomi-san
at college in forever

02:20.990 --> 02:23.330
He does this often,
so don't worry.
Cheer up!

02:20.990 --> 02:23.330
Okay

02:22.120 --> 02:29.290
Thanks! I'll hang in there!

02:22.120 --> 02:29.290
<b>Today</b>

02:22.120 --> 02:29.290
On the next Rockin' Robin
day off, I'm gonna go shopping
for supplies with the boss.

02:23.640 --> 02:28.650
<i>On the next Rockin' Robin day off, I'm gonna 
go shopping for supplies with the boss.</i>

02:29.780 --> 02:32.920
<i>What? Way to go, Rin-chan!</i>

02:32.210 --> 02:42.550
What? Way to go,
Rin-chan!

02:34.450 --> 02:35.710
<i>But...</i>

02:34.670 --> 02:42.550
But...

02:35.710 --> 02:37.000
<i>Instant reply!</i>

02:38.550 --> 02:42.550
I don't think I could
handle being alone
in a car with him yet...

02:38.640 --> 02:42.820
<i>I don't think I could handle 
being alone in a car with him yet...</i>

02:43.600 --> 02:49.560
So why don't you and Itsuomi-san join us?

02:43.890 --> 02:47.400
<i>So why don't you and Itsuomi-san join us?</i>

02:47.400 --> 02:48.760
<i>All four of us?</i>

02:50.370 --> 02:53.440
<i>Itsuomi-san and I did make plans to meet up.</i>

02:53.440 --> 02:55.770
<i>Maybe we could do this instead?</i>

02:57.170 --> 03:03.270
<i>I may feel like I could go anywhere, 
but there's only one place I want to go.</i>

03:04.440 --> 03:07.260
<i>Okay, I'll try asking him!</i>

03:11.290 --> 03:12.340
Let me sleep over.

03:12.990 --> 03:17.640
Yeah... I'm not gonna ask why. 
I already know, more or less.

03:17.640 --> 03:20.310
Also, I'm kinda hungry.

03:21.760 --> 03:24.220
<i>Objection! There is no evidence 
supporting this claim!</i>

03:24.640 --> 03:26.540
<i>Objection sustained.</i>

03:24.930 --> 03:27.290
Can I switch to the subtitled 
version for this movie?

03:26.950 --> 03:30.730
<i>Do you mind if I ask you 
a couple of questions, ma'am?</i>

03:27.290 --> 03:30.730
You always do. Feel free.

03:31.810 --> 03:35.100
<i>Are you sure that you haven't 
seen them for the time being?</i>

03:32.900 --> 03:36.410
Are you sure that you haven't 
seen them for the time being?

03:36.410 --> 03:39.840
What's it called, shadowing? 
That thing where you repeat what's said.

03:36.690 --> 03:40.440
<i>To tell the truth, a woman 
testified that she saw you, him,</i>

03:39.840 --> 03:40.860
Yep.

03:40.440 --> 03:43.160
<i>and the men in the shop 
two hours before the incident.</i>

03:41.150 --> 03:45.230
You're keeping that up 
even though you're fluent?

03:43.160 --> 03:45.240
<i>And the other person who was there</i>

03:45.230 --> 03:48.060
You forget the languages 
you don't use frequently.

03:45.240 --> 03:48.010
<i>gave us information that you were 
quarreling for a while.</i>

03:48.060 --> 03:49.370
Huh...

03:48.520 --> 03:50.140
<i>Please give us the truth...</i>

03:50.140 --> 03:51.530
<i>Have you seen them?</i>

03:50.140 --> 03:54.380
I guess there are no shortcuts 
for plain old effort.

03:51.530 --> 03:54.380
<i>Your Honor, may I summon 
the partner for questioning?</i>

04:01.010 --> 04:03.280
<i>How many gunshots did you hear?</i>

04:03.280 --> 04:05.120
<i>Two? Three?</i>

04:05.120 --> 04:06.150
<i>Or more?</i>

04:07.890 --> 04:09.840
Is that sign?

04:09.840 --> 04:10.810
"More."

04:11.380 --> 04:13.430
Yuki-chan taught you that, huh?

04:15.140 --> 04:18.770
You know, unlike with English and stuff,

04:18.770 --> 04:22.150
she's the only one you can use 
sign language with right now.

04:22.670 --> 04:25.230
So why are you trying to learn it?

04:26.210 --> 04:27.930
Is that for your dream, too?

04:30.160 --> 04:33.360
<i>Yuki-chan seemed to be into Itsu.</i>

04:33.360 --> 04:35.200
<i>There's the Emma-chan mess, too.</i>

04:35.200 --> 04:38.410
<i>I really don't wanna see these girls crying.</i>

04:39.420 --> 04:41.100
Beer for you.

04:41.990 --> 04:44.170
Uh, it was mine to begin with.

04:44.170 --> 04:47.430
<b>Sat</b>

04:48.760 --> 04:52.200
Huh? You made plans with Rin?

04:52.640 --> 04:54.080
Why?

04:54.080 --> 04:57.560
Yuki just asked if I wanted to join you guys.

04:57.870 --> 05:01.450
Oh, right. You wanna come along 
on the shopping run?

05:01.450 --> 05:02.690
Oho?

05:02.960 --> 05:04.570
Rin, huh?

05:04.570 --> 05:08.200
What? There's nothing going on with her!

05:12.160 --> 05:13.910
Rin-chan just asked if
we wanted to join them

05:12.160 --> 05:13.910
Why don't we go together?

05:14.580 --> 05:16.670
Sure

06:06.380 --> 06:09.210
Wow, that girl was so pretty!

06:09.210 --> 06:11.310
I saw that, too! Think she's a model?

06:11.310 --> 06:13.140
Her hair is out of this world!

06:19.800 --> 06:22.110
How you doin', babe? Where are you headed?

06:22.430 --> 06:23.920
You meeting up with anybody?

06:23.920 --> 06:25.880
Uh, a friend? Well?

06:26.500 --> 06:28.090
Hello? Don't ignore me.

06:29.910 --> 06:33.390
Oh? Who are you calling?

06:33.390 --> 06:34.840
A friend.

06:34.840 --> 06:36.370
For real? Is she cute?

06:37.460 --> 06:38.870
It's a guy!

06:52.000 --> 06:53.460
Thank you. Come again.

06:58.140 --> 07:01.150
Night

06:58.140 --> 07:01.150
Today

06:58.140 --> 07:01.150
Shin-chaaan

06:58.140 --> 07:01.150
When do you get off work today?

06:58.140 --> 07:01.150
I'm in the mood for some good booze!

07:07.650 --> 07:09.650
I'm down

07:08.310 --> 07:09.650
Thank you for waiting.

07:09.960 --> 07:12.040
Here's your beef skirt steak.

07:12.410 --> 07:15.910
That looks so good!

07:17.880 --> 07:21.610
It's great! You should try it, Shin-chan!

07:21.610 --> 07:22.420
I will.

07:22.420 --> 07:25.600
Say, how about we get 
another bottle of red wine?

07:25.600 --> 07:27.570
Whoa, you really are in the mood.

07:27.570 --> 07:28.920
What's wrong, Emma?

07:29.320 --> 07:30.480
Itsu-kun again?

07:30.480 --> 07:34.180
Sure is. I put myself out there, 
and he didn't even blink!

07:34.180 --> 07:38.560
And for some reason, 
he's studying something again.

07:38.560 --> 07:39.680
Studying what?

07:39.680 --> 07:43.720
Well... sign language or something?

07:43.720 --> 07:44.860
Wow.

07:44.860 --> 07:48.190
Sheesh. My heart was about to explode.

07:49.080 --> 07:50.870
Well, gotta drink and forget it all.

07:51.460 --> 07:53.960
Excuse me! We'll have 
another bottle of red wine!

07:53.960 --> 07:57.200
I knew I could count on you to have my back!

07:57.500 --> 07:59.480
I'll drink with you all you want tonight.

07:59.480 --> 08:02.210
Stahp! I could cry!

08:02.650 --> 08:05.910
I'm <i>so</i> glad you're here for me!

08:07.830 --> 08:11.240
Okay, let's eat. This looks amazing.

08:11.240 --> 08:16.010
And eat I will! Itsu-kun, you jerk!

08:24.930 --> 08:26.980
<i>Today's the day.</i>

08:28.440 --> 08:32.040
<i>I'm feeling the butterflies, 
both good and bad.</i>

08:32.040 --> 08:34.550
<i>I hope we can get everyone 
involved in fun convos.</i>

08:35.560 --> 08:39.710
<i>Rin-chan said she and the boss 
would come pick me up by car,</i>

08:39.710 --> 08:42.650
<i>but I'd feel bad asking them 
to come all the way to my place.</i>

08:43.410 --> 08:48.420
<i>Besides, I didn't want Oushi-kun to see me, 
like he did the other night.</i>

08:52.800 --> 08:53.510
<i>Why...</i>

08:53.510 --> 08:55.500
<i>Why are you here?!</i>

08:55.500 --> 08:58.760
What's up with that reaction? 
And where are you going?

08:58.760 --> 09:00.410
<i>Calm down...</i>

09:01.270 --> 09:02.930
<i>To the library.</i>

09:03.230 --> 09:04.760
The library?

09:04.760 --> 09:07.910
<i>By the way, what time 
did you get back last time?</i>

09:09.060 --> 09:10.020
Hey!

09:11.540 --> 09:15.480
<i>He comes off so childish 
compared to Itsuomi-san.</i>

09:52.290 --> 09:53.370
<i>You're heavy.</i>

09:54.820 --> 09:58.070
Today

09:54.820 --> 09:58.070
I'm right outside the gates

09:54.940 --> 09:58.070
Okay

09:55.430 --> 09:57.450
<i>Oh, it's Itsuomi-san.</i>

09:59.590 --> 10:02.150
This isn't the stop for the library.

10:02.150 --> 10:03.580
Hey, Yuki.

10:05.120 --> 10:07.080
<i>So many people out today!</i>

10:07.560 --> 10:10.210
Yuki! Hold up!

10:11.540 --> 10:13.400
<i>Where's Itsuomi-san?</i>

10:14.840 --> 10:15.930
Yuki!

10:20.450 --> 10:21.700
Target acquired.

10:23.380 --> 10:24.350
Yuki.

10:27.600 --> 10:29.240
<i>Oushi-kun...</i>

10:29.240 --> 10:31.610
<i>You're here to meet up with </i>him<i>?</i>

10:32.020 --> 10:33.820
<b>Hmph.</b>

10:32.020 --> 10:33.820
<b>Hmph.</b>

10:32.870 --> 10:33.770
Hey!

10:33.770 --> 10:34.480
What?

10:46.130 --> 10:52.380
She can't hear, so you should try 
not to grab her from behind.

10:52.760 --> 10:54.460
<i>I can't read his lips.</i>

10:55.880 --> 10:58.520
<i>Is he saying something?</i>

11:00.280 --> 11:01.640
Yuki said...

11:02.320 --> 11:04.510
It's okay if it's me.

11:05.540 --> 11:06.540
Wha?

11:27.060 --> 11:30.980
<i>Huh? Why's he glaring so angrily?!</i>

11:32.050 --> 11:34.330
<i>He's glaring at Itsuomi-san.</i>

11:40.340 --> 11:41.940
<i>Itsuomi-san...</i>

11:47.090 --> 11:48.820
It's nothing.

11:49.860 --> 11:50.930
Let's go.

11:56.370 --> 11:58.220
<i>"Nothing"?</i>

11:58.220 --> 12:00.380
<i>It sure didn't feel like nothing.</i>

12:04.760 --> 12:05.820
<i>"You."</i>

12:06.640 --> 12:07.540
<i>"Fool."</i>

12:08.280 --> 12:12.020
<i>What? Why?</i>

12:13.840 --> 12:17.430
<i>Itsuomi-san still seems kinda mad.</i>

12:18.750 --> 12:21.630
Did something happen?

12:21.960 --> 12:23.480
Don't worry about it.

12:23.480 --> 12:25.630
We guys have our own stuff going on.

12:25.630 --> 12:26.640
<i>Oh.</i>

12:27.000 --> 12:30.230
<i>I get the feeling I shouldn't pry any further.</i>

12:47.480 --> 12:48.410
Oh...

12:48.410 --> 12:51.410
Looks like they'll be here soon.

12:48.410 --> 12:51.410
Nerves!

12:48.410 --> 12:51.410
Hurry up, Yuki!

12:48.410 --> 12:51.410
I just got to the station
and met up with Itsuomi-san.

12:48.410 --> 12:51.410
We're heading over now.

12:51.410 --> 12:53.800
Really? That was fast.

12:55.040 --> 12:56.640
Right?

12:56.640 --> 13:01.400
<i>I can't handle this situation! Hurry up, Yuki!</i>

13:01.400 --> 13:02.920
I'm glad it's so perfect out.

13:02.920 --> 13:04.230
You said it!

13:06.920 --> 13:10.520
<i>I'm so sad he had to resort 
to talking about the weather!</i>

13:10.520 --> 13:12.830
<i>You better spice things up, girl!</i>

13:12.830 --> 13:17.690
By the way, Kyouya-san, 
this place opened up nearby...

13:18.060 --> 13:20.700
<i>Did he just sigh? End me now!</i>

13:21.500 --> 13:26.300
Say, Rin-chan... I dunno if this 
is appropriate to ask, but...

13:27.680 --> 13:31.320
Does Yuki-chan like Itsu?

13:31.320 --> 13:33.200
Or is she interested in him, at least?

13:34.370 --> 13:37.340
The guy's hot. And popular.

13:37.890 --> 13:42.260
But right now, he's more interested 
in chasing his dreams than romance.

13:42.820 --> 13:44.970
His dreams...?

13:44.970 --> 13:51.500
Yeah. And I've seen so many of our female 
customers cry after he rejected them.

13:52.060 --> 13:54.760
Are you worried Yuki's 
going to end up like them?

13:55.830 --> 13:56.730
Yeah...

13:57.130 --> 14:00.960
But don't you think he's taken a liking to her?

14:00.960 --> 14:03.580
He seems really interested 
in learning sign, too.

14:04.240 --> 14:08.840
If he's taken a liking to her as a potential 
partner, I'll be over the moon, too...

14:10.870 --> 14:16.250
But I wonder where the affection 
he shows her is coming from, really.

14:19.860 --> 14:22.520
Rin-chan, looks like they're here.

14:24.160 --> 14:25.580
What?!

14:25.580 --> 14:26.570
We're here.

14:26.570 --> 14:29.630
Wait, time out! Why are you holding hands?!

14:29.930 --> 14:34.460
Hmm? Because Yuki nearly 
got run over back there.

14:34.460 --> 14:36.640
Oh... Is that so...

14:36.940 --> 14:38.490
Glad she's okay.

14:38.490 --> 14:39.660
Anyway, hop in.

14:39.660 --> 14:40.440
'Kay.

14:51.650 --> 14:53.160
We're good to go, Kyouya.

14:53.160 --> 14:55.950
A-A-All right! Shall we get going?

14:55.950 --> 14:56.910
Yeah!

14:56.910 --> 15:00.180
Let's go!

15:08.040 --> 15:10.300
What are you looking to buy today?

15:10.300 --> 15:14.220
Aside from bar supplies, I'm also 
going to pick up some personal stuff.

15:14.220 --> 15:16.180
So feel free to look around yourself, Rin-chan.

15:16.430 --> 15:18.930
<i>Kyouya-san's so nice!</i>

15:19.480 --> 15:22.880
What kind of personal stuff?

15:22.880 --> 15:26.940
Well, I love rice seasoning, 
so I'm gonna pick up big bags of those.

15:26.940 --> 15:29.690
<i>Kyouya-san's so cute!</i>

16:03.130 --> 16:04.850
Whoa!

16:05.180 --> 16:07.590
These snack bags are huge!

16:08.310 --> 16:10.610
It makes me happy to see you all excited, too.

16:16.240 --> 16:17.620
Yuki.

16:21.360 --> 16:23.370
<i>What's gotten into these two?</i>

16:25.680 --> 16:29.130
<i>Wow, tiramisu! It's so big!</i>

16:30.210 --> 16:32.280
It makes you look tiny, Yuki.

16:32.770 --> 16:34.410
Do you want this?

16:44.810 --> 16:46.900
Notes

16:44.810 --> 16:46.900
Done

16:44.810 --> 16:46.900
What was that earlier?

16:46.900 --> 16:49.460
Uh, well...

16:50.360 --> 16:51.650
Oh.

16:52.820 --> 16:54.900
Don't tell Itsu.

16:55.280 --> 17:00.330
But when he called for you, 
his voice had a super affectionate tone.

17:04.300 --> 17:05.620
<i>Really?</i>

17:06.290 --> 17:09.820
<i>I didn't know voices could 
be so obviously different.</i>

17:11.090 --> 17:12.330
What?

17:12.330 --> 17:13.660
Nothing.

17:15.600 --> 17:18.680
<i>What kind of voice does he usually have?</i>

17:19.430 --> 17:22.490
<i>Was that the only time he's 
spoken to me affectionately?</i>

17:22.490 --> 17:27.930
<i>Or has he always done that?</i>

17:28.760 --> 17:30.440
<i>Yeah, right. As if.</i>

17:35.540 --> 17:36.950
This chocolate's great.

17:37.520 --> 17:38.670
It's Belgian.

17:38.670 --> 17:40.450
<i>It looks great!</i>

17:40.900 --> 17:42.980
You'll pick some up, right? Right?

17:43.430 --> 17:45.210
<i>A pushy sales pitch!</i>

17:54.370 --> 17:58.580
<i>Oh, wow... I'm having such a great time today.</i>

18:02.480 --> 18:05.850
Have you ever been overseas, Yuki?

18:08.980 --> 18:14.360
But I've been told that a lot of deaf
people get hooked on foreign travel
because they have an easier time
communicating with gestures.

18:12.870 --> 18:14.360
I see.

18:14.930 --> 18:20.550
Makes sense. The desire to communicate 
is what really matters.

18:22.370 --> 18:25.800
<i>That feeling can show the way.</i>

18:25.800 --> 18:27.130
It goes for you too, Yuki.

18:29.060 --> 18:34.950
When we first met, you had this look in your 
eyes when you signed "Thank you" to me.

18:35.810 --> 18:39.160
I still can't seem to forget it.

18:40.130 --> 18:45.140
Back when I couldn't speak English and had 
a message I really wanted to get across,

18:45.140 --> 18:47.660
I thought that maybe I had 
a similar look in my eyes.

18:48.150 --> 18:52.180
<i>I had no idea he felt that way.</i>

18:53.730 --> 18:55.650
All right.

18:56.400 --> 19:00.230
Next time I go overseas, 
I'll take you with me in my carry bag.

19:00.710 --> 19:02.680
Would you mind jumping in?

19:02.680 --> 19:04.410
<i>Is that...</i>

19:04.720 --> 19:07.580
<i>an invitation to go together?</i>

19:08.040 --> 19:11.670
I don't want to be
unneeded baggage.

19:10.640 --> 19:11.670
Just kidding.

19:12.900 --> 19:14.670
You won't be.

19:18.520 --> 19:24.380
<i>Everything he says shoots me 
right through the heart.</i>

19:25.090 --> 19:28.620
<i>What kind of voice did he say that in?</i>

19:35.150 --> 19:38.190
Is Kyouya-san going to be all right?

19:38.660 --> 19:41.950
Maybe I should go help him.

19:45.350 --> 19:46.180
Rin.

19:47.740 --> 19:50.040
What is it, Itsuomi-san?

19:50.040 --> 19:52.570
Should we give you and Kyouya 
some alone time on the way back?

19:52.570 --> 19:53.580
Huh?!

19:54.120 --> 19:58.510
So that's why you've been 
coming to the bar a lot lately.

19:58.510 --> 20:01.470
Wh-Whatever could you mean?

20:01.470 --> 20:04.300
Be honest. Then I'll help you out.

20:04.300 --> 20:06.220
Counting on you!

20:06.220 --> 20:07.450
Okay.

20:08.280 --> 20:11.230
Tell him to take you 
on a drive on the way back.

20:11.230 --> 20:14.380
What? Weren't you gonna help me out?

20:14.380 --> 20:15.880
I just gave you some advice.

20:15.880 --> 20:17.230
What if he says no?!

20:17.550 --> 20:20.780
Finally. Sorry, there was a huge line.

20:20.780 --> 20:22.480
Kyouya-san!

20:22.480 --> 20:23.530
Go for it.

20:23.530 --> 20:24.300
C'mon.

20:28.600 --> 20:31.680
Looks like those two are gonna 
go for a drive on the way home.

20:31.680 --> 20:32.790
<i>Huh?</i>

20:32.790 --> 20:35.880
<i>Wow, Rin-chan's going for it today.</i>

20:38.320 --> 20:41.930
<i>Cute. I'm happy for you, Rin-chan.</i>

20:41.930 --> 20:47.050
Shall we leave our stuff with them 
and take the train back?

20:47.050 --> 20:50.580
<i>Oh, right. We'll be alone 
on the way back, too.</i>

20:53.060 --> 20:56.060
Later. You do your best too, Yuki.

20:59.380 --> 21:00.470
Shall we?

21:17.710 --> 21:18.540
Hmm?

21:20.710 --> 21:21.750
What?

21:27.100 --> 21:28.570
"You and me."

21:31.190 --> 21:33.000
"Shall we get dinner together?"

21:33.920 --> 21:37.110
Oh, hey, I'm starting to get the hang of sign.

21:41.080 --> 21:43.600
I'm going home.

21:43.600 --> 21:44.990
<i>He shot me down!</i>

21:44.990 --> 21:46.820
<i>Sadness!</i>

21:49.330 --> 21:50.990
Why not eat at my place?

21:52.340 --> 21:53.240
<i>Place?</i>

21:53.520 --> 21:54.790
Kyouya?

21:54.210 --> 21:56.920
<i>Like, his place of residence?</i>

21:54.790 --> 21:57.470
On second thought, I think we'll take 
the pizzas and stuff with us.

21:57.470 --> 21:59.000
Are you still nearby?

21:57.470 --> 21:59.160
<i>Hold on a second.</i>

21:59.160 --> 22:02.500
<i>Does that mean...</i>

21:59.460 --> 22:01.770
Yeah, gotcha. Thanks.

